After Asha leaves, the door closes.
Moti is very nervous.
He paces around the whole flat.
He goes near the door and whines.
I feel very bad for him.
I sit on my rug placed on the floor.
I pat the rug with my hand.
I say to him affectionately, 'Moti, come here.'
'Sit here near me.'
But he does not come.
I look in Moti's bag.
His favorite chew toy is there.
I take out that toy.
I show the toy to Moti.
I say to him, 'Moti, take this.'
'Come here and hold this.'
He looks at the toy and comes towards me.
He sits down on the rug near me.
He takes the toy and chews it happily.
Now he is completely calm.
